## Context
PR #1037 (ticket 0568) added a per-agent memory-vs-web comparison and per-agent multi-turn deltas to §exp2 as inline F1 literals guarded by re-derivation tests (tests/test_manuscript_claims_alignment.py), following the established pattern (tickets 0515/0501/0474). The verify-gate flagged the tension with the numbers-through-macros rule (ticket 0531, .claude/rules/writing.md). Orchestrator ruling 2026-06-12: guard pattern accepted for the PR; strict-macro uniformity deferred here. Related: open ticket 0566 covers the same conversion for the hand-typed ρ = 0.92.

## Actions
Extend the emitter that owns the exp2 fragment (see MANUSCRIPT_MACRO_FRAGMENTS in experiments/render.mk) to emit macros for all five §exp2 literal-pair sites (the four pre-existing equalization pairs included); replace inline literals with the macros; keep the re-derivation tests as cross-checks; coordinate with 0566 (same emitters) — consider executing both in one PR.

## Raid plan notes (2026-06-12)

- Site count clarified: 4 paragraph-level sites in §exp2 (relocate by grep):
  (1) per-agent memory-vs-web comparison (~727-730, PR #1037);
  (2) per-agent multi-turn no-docs deltas (~800-802, PR #1037);
  (3) documents-equalization paragraph (~827-833, 4 agent pairs + spread
  values + convergence target, pre-existing);
  (4) multi-turn-with-docs degradation (~837-838, pre-existing).
  Convert ALL inline F1 literals in these four paragraphs.
- No exp2 F1 fragment exists yet. Owner: `tabulate_exp2_2x2.py` (already
  computes per-agent arm means from committed `tab_exp2_2x2.csv` via
  `collapse_runs()`). Add `write_macros()` + `--output-macros`, upgrade the
  Makefile rule (render.mk ~421-437) to a grouped `&:` rule, add the new
  fragment `macros_exp2_2x2` to `MANUSCRIPT_MACRO_FRAGMENTS`.
- Cover all four arms (naive, optimised, arm3, arm4) — the equalization
  paragraph uses documents-arm values.
- Naming: flat scalar macros, distinct prefix from the existing
  `\ExpTwo*Matrix*` names, e.g. `\ExpTwoFOneAnthropicNaive`. The
  duplicate-name guard (render.mk ~749-754) catches collisions at build.
- `test_manuscript_claims_alignment.py` needs no edits: it checks
  `normalized()` output, which expands macros. Keep as cross-checks.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] no inline F1 literal pairs in §exp2
